      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Logging**\n\nOkay, I've decided to go with Google Cloud Logging for this task. It's a managed service, which simplifies things. The next step is to figure out the specific Python libraries and configurations to integrate with it, ensuring the JSON log format aligns correctly with the service's expectations.\n\n\n**Defining Log Structure**\n\nNow I am creating the `write_structured_log.py` file. I'm focusing on the file's basic structure and how to begin structuring the log event. I'll start by importing the necessary Google Cloud Logging library. Then I will establish a function to format and write the structured log event. This will involve handling a dictionary-formatted log event and an optional log name.\n\n\n",
